// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from this index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this index is null, or the element at the next position equals the old element at this index.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the current size inclusive, then for every index from this index to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent position is either null if the previous was null or equal to the previous element.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list inclusive), then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index is either both null or equal to the element at the previous index before the insertion.
